      "commit_id": "d92473f1f023fc1599bc171d0c15f1daa0a777d2",
      "immutable": false,
      "summary": "Installer runs Dafny and Boogie on hosts with only .NET 10",
      "body": "On Ubuntu 26.04 only the .NET 10 runtime is packaged, and Boogie (built for .NET 8) refuses to start. When no .NET 8 runtime is present, install.sh now writes launchers for dafny and boogie into ~/.local/bin, ahead of ~/.dotnet/tools on PATH, that set DOTNET_ROLL_FORWARD=Major. gh_asset also now prints nothing (rather than the string \"null\") when no release asset matches, so a fallback written as $(a || b) receives only the other URL. Verified on a fresh Ubuntu 26.04.1 VM with only Microsoft.NETCore.App 10.0.14: bash -n passes, dafny --version reports 4.11.0 and boogie starts through the launcher, and the new jq filter returns the first matching URL or exits 4 with no output on a sample release JSON.",
      "log_sha256": "584c77f06146c3e893761af0bedfc3c6c7abc1b6642bb2538f8281b9a0dbed78"
    },
